  "title": "The two connected quandles of order 6 colour every knot equally",
  "subject": "Colourings of classical knots by the conjugation quandles of S4",
  "conclusion": "Every S4 transposition colouring of a knot has trivial longitude, and over each S3 colouring the twisted lifting cohomology meets the boundary torus in a line over the meridian (half-lives-half-dies), so transposition and 4-cycle lifts are equinumerous. Hence the connected quandles C[6,1] and C[6,2] colour every classical knot equally, proving the 2013 conjecture of Clark, Elhamdadi, Hou, Saito and Yeatman for this pair; a virtual knot shows the 3-manifold input is needed.",
